# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Iced Intentions — environment variables
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` for local dev, and set the same keys in Vercel
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) for production.
#
# ⚠️  EVERYTHING PREFIXED `VITE_` IS BUNDLED INTO THE PUBLIC JAVASCRIPT
#     AND IS VISIBLE TO ANYONE. Only ever put publishable/anon keys here.
#     Secrets (Square access token, service role key) belong in Supabase
#     Edge Function secrets — never in this file.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Supabase (required) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ── Square payments (required — card payment is the only checkout) ──
# Developer dashboard → your app → Credentials
# Without these, the site blocks checkout rather than take unpayable orders.
VITE_SQUARE_APP_ID=your-square-application-id
VITE_SQUARE_LOCATION_ID=your-square-location-id
VITE_SQUARE_ENV=sandbox          # sandbox | production

# ── Email ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing goes here. Email is sent server-side by the `send-email` Edge
# Function via Resend, so the sending key is never exposed to the browser.
# Set these as SUPABASE EDGE FUNCTION SECRETS instead (Dashboard →
# Edge Functions → Secrets, or `supabase secrets set`):
#
#   RESEND_API_KEY   re_xxxxxxxxxx
#   RESEND_FROM      Iced Intentions <hello@yourdomain.com>
#   OWNER_EMAIL      you@yourdomain.com
#
# The same place already holds the Square secrets:
#   SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN, SQUARE_LOCATION_ID, SQUARE_ENV

# ── Business details shown on the site (optional) ──────────────
VITE_BUSINESS_PHONE=(661) 555-0142
VITE_BUSINESS_ADDRESS=Bakersfield, CA
VITE_BUSINESS_INSTAGRAM=@iced.intentions_
